Keep ltp_buffer_state within the layout of the current frame.

The decoder toggles ltp_buffer_state by XOR with frameLength (plain AAC)
or frameLength + 288 (SBR), so a stream that switches between the two
leaves values such as 288 or 1024 during an SBR frame. sbr_dec() then
copies 288 samples to ltp_buffer[state - 1312], before the buffer, which
overwrote mc_info.bDownSampledSbr in the decoder state. The toggle is now
explicit, an SBR frame restarts from 0 when the state does not match its
layout, and long-term prediction (which assumes an offset of at most
frameLength) is skipped for the SBR layout.

